    <briefdescription>
<para>This class represents an assumption made on an AddRec expression. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Given an affine AddRec expression {a,+,b}, we assume that it has the nssw or nusw flags (defined below) in the first X iterations of the loop, where X is a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_s_c_e_v" kindref="compound">SCEV</ref> expression returned by getPredicatedBackedgeTakenCount).</para>
<para>Note that this does not imply that X is equal to the backedge taken count. This means that if we have a nusw predicate for i32 {0,+,1} with a predicated backedge taken count of X, we only guarantee that {0,+,1} has nusw in the first X iterations. {0,+,1} may still wrap in the loop if we have more than X iterations. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
